I’ll inspect the specimen metadata, pattern, and the frozen analysis package first, then build and refine the smallest physically supported phase model. I’ll keep the final exports tied to one replay-stable GSAS-II project and reserve the mandated bounded polish for the terminal model.

The chemistry points first to Ba–W–O products, but the task deliberately permits incomplete reaction and multiple crystalline products. I’m now extracting the exact laboratory parameter ranges and the polish acceptance rules so that phase search and refinement do not absorb missing peaks into unphysical profile or calibration terms.

Three coherent reflection families are already apparent:

