The polish branches are converging without bound hits. All three coordinate paths are landing in essentially the same basin (Rwp ≈3.119% after cell/scale/background replay), with phase fractions stable to well under 1% relative.

The polish audit selects the heavy→light branch. It is eligible, converged (max shift/esd 0.0050), has no frozen variables or geometry violations, and preserves fractions; the read-only replay confirms Rwp 3.1187%, normalized fractions, finite profile arrays, nonnegative background, and no active refinement flags. I’m accepting it as the exact submitted project and exporting all deliverables read-only from that file.

